        "original_id": "b5285ed7-ad45-5d1e-b91a-53c2fb721600",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Howard Hawks, Arthur Berthelet, Katharine Hepburn, Cary Grant, Bessie Love\n- Films: Bringing Up Baby, Penny of Top Hill Trail\n- Companies: RKO Radio Pictures\n- Roles: film director, producer, screenwriter\n\nFacts:\n- Howard Hawks was born on May 30, 1896, and he was an American film director, producer, and screenwriter of the classic Hollywood era.\n- Arthur Berthelet was born in 1879, and he was an American film director who moved from directing stage plays, including several on Broadway, to directing silent movies.\n- Bringing Up Baby is a 1938 American screwball comedy film directed by Howard Hawks, starring Katharine Hepburn and Cary Grant, and released by RKO Radio Pictures.\n- Penny of Top Hill Trail was directed by Arthur Berthelet and starred Bessie Love.\n- Arthur Berthelet died in 1949.\n- Howard Hawks died on December 26, 1977.",
